{"id": "tea:satyayani-upanisad:12-17", "source": "src:satyayani-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "12-17"}, "paraphrase": "The renouncer's sacrifices are inner: japa, the yoga of service to Hari and guru, austerity as non-injury, study of the Upaniṣads, and the sacrifice of knowledge, the best; knowledge is his staff, topknot and thread.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "ethics"], "concepts": ["cpt:inner-sacrifice"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text satyayani-upanisad 12-17"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 12-17 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'trisandhyaṃ śaktitaḥ snānaṃ tarpaṇaṃ mārjanaṃ tathā | upasthānaṃ pañcayajñānkuryādāmara-ṇāntikam || 12 ||…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:satyayani-upanisad:26-29", "source": "src:satyayani-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "26-29"}, "paraphrase": "One who abandons this Vaiṣṇava discipline is like a killer of heroes and brāhmaṇas, not purified even by expiations — one who has fallen from the height.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ethics", "dispute"], "disputes": ["dsp:renunciant-marks-ekadanda-tridanda"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text satyayani-upanisad 26-29"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 26-29 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'atha khalu somyedaṃ pārivrājyaṃ naiṣṭhikamātmadharmaṃ yovijahāti sa vīrahā bhavati | sa brahmahā bhavati | sa…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:satyayani-upanisad:30-32", "source": "src:satyayani-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "30-32"}, "paraphrase": "The renouncer uplifts a hundred generations before and three hundred after; even uttering 'I have renounced' with the last breath in the throat saves the ancestors.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["death-dying", "karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:sannyasa-rite"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text satyayani-upanisad 30-32"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 30-32 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'atha khalusomyemaṃ sanātanamātmadharmaṃ vaiṣṇavīṃ niṣṭhāṃ labdhvā yastāmadūṣayanvartate sa vaśībhavati | sa…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:satyayani-upanisad:6-8", "source": "src:satyayani-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "6-8"}, "paraphrase": "Triple staff, thread, cloth or loincloth with girdle, sling and strainer — these he keeps till death, and is buried with them.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ethics", "death-dying"], "concepts": ["cpt:renunciant-marks"], "disputes": ["dsp:renunciant-marks-ekadanda-tridanda"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text satyayani-upanisad 6-8"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 6-8 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'tyakteṣaṇo hyanṛṇastaṃ viditvā maunī vasedāśrameyatra kutra | athāśramaṃ caramaṃ sampraviśya yathopapattiṃ…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:satyayani-upanisad:9-11", "source": "src:satyayani-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "9-11"}, "paraphrase": "Viṣṇu's mark is twofold, manifest and unmanifest; abandoning either one falls; the triple staff is the Vaiṣṇava mark. All four kinds of renouncer bear Viṣṇu's mark, topknot and thread, and perform the five sacrifices; they differ in livelihood.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ethics", "dispute"], "concepts": ["cpt:renunciant-marks", "cpt:four-kinds-of-sannyasa"], "disputes": ["dsp:renunciant-marks-ekadanda-tridanda"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text satyayani-upanisad 9-11"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 9-11 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'viṣṇuliṅgaṃ dvidhā proktaṃ vyaktamavyaktamevaca | tayorekamapi tyaktvā patatyeva na saṃśayaḥ || 9 ||…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
